  "worked_solution": "To raise a power to another power, we simply multiply the exponents:\n\n$$\n{({9}^{3})}^{-6}={9}^{3\\cdot (-6)}={9}^{-18}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate ${9}^{-18},$ we find the reciprocal of the base $(9)$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{9}^{-18}={(\\frac{1}{9})}^{18}\n$$",
